-- Indexes for every foreign key that had no leading index.
--
-- 164 of 275 foreign keys were unindexed while 210 of them use ON DELETE RESTRICT.
-- Without a leading index on the referencing column, PostgreSQL scans the whole
-- child table (and locks it) on every parent delete or key update, and RLS
-- policies filtering by project_id fall back to sequential scans.
--
-- Plain CREATE INDEX rather than CONCURRENTLY: migrations run inside a
-- transaction, and every table here is still small enough that the lock is
-- negligible. Revisit if this ever has to be applied to a loaded database.

